      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T20:34:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Tom,\n\nI benchmarked PdfDocument() init (which calls LoadPages() -\u003e CountPages()) across a few PDFs ranging from 37KB/1 page to 43MB/754 pages, 20 iterations each:\n\n  - 754 pages: 6.29ms median\n  - 492 pages: 0.36ms median\n  - 85 pages: 0.13ms median\n  - 1 page: 0.13ms median\n\nThe /Kids traversal in CountPages() is O(pages) and runs once at document init. \n\nFor this 754-page reference manual, the overhead is under 7ms. The cost is dominated by I/O and parsing, not page tree walking. This one had a complex page structure: https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/reference-manual/MCF5235RM.pdf",
      "parentUuid": "c86df45a_784b7180",
      "revId": "dc6ed04fe6aba14ea0282995126dafeba9dadfb6",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "990eca88_6af63069",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T21:10:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have some version of the ARM architecture manual laying around. This copy is only 78 MB but has 12940 pages. My micro-benchmark is:\n\n```\nTEST_F(FPDFViewEmbedderTest, Foo) {\n  ASSERT_TRUE(OpenDocument(\"arm.pdf\"));\n  EXPECT_EQ(12940, FPDF_GetPageCount(document()));\n}\n```\n\nIn a release build without V8, it\u0027s ~100 ms without this CL vs. 250 ms with.",
      "parentUuid": "be3d7805_82589c62",
      "revId": "dc6ed04fe6aba14ea0282995126dafeba9dadfb6",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
